  "subtitle": "Proximal Humerus Fractures Updated: Jun 9 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 humerus plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Humerus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Humerus Posterior (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Extra Articular Distal Humerus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423194/images/9cbed5cb-48ec-4562-b876-9df36e27787c_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.49.12_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept non-locking screws, and locking screws with a 30° cone.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**7mm Oblong K-wire Slot**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Assists with proximal / distal plate positioning.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423194/images/33ff7e47-d123-4844-b651-59b77c88a4fb_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.48.15_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Straight Anterior Plate Contour**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Helps to ensure reduction with the bicipital groove.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**8mm Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in desired plate placement and serve as an attachment site for targeter.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**3 variable angle calcar screw holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Provides additional flexibility to achieve screw placement in the calcar bone of varying fracture patterns and patient morphologies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423194/images/33ff7e47-d123-4844-b651-59b77c88a4fb_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.48.15_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted scalloped shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Reduced potential for periosteal disturbance while maintaining strength of plate and final construct",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Designed to improve tuberosity fixation and prevent tuberosity escape",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed to increase fixation by providing an option for perpendicular screw placement in the setting of tuberosity fractures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Extension arms are designed to facilitate in-situ contouring to capture tuberosity fragments.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Humerus Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of humerus bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard deltopectoral or deltoid split approach to the proximal humerus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Posterior plate lengths: 3-8 holes (86-161mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: 3.2mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
